00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:37.000
Noam Wolf: what is… what are the next steps? I do feel like I want to know… have the control, because I have the… I have my bot, and it's doing for me everything already. Like, it's blog posts 3 times a week, it writes them and it uploads it to the website, it makes design changes on my website.

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.000
Whitney Hodges: Yes.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:37.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:53.000
Noam Wolf: and updates, like, new logos of, you know, past clients and stuff like that within 2 seconds, and I don't have to put any effort into it, because I already gave it access to everything, and… so it's great. I don't want to be… I want to know how to do it so I can teach my bot, and then…

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:18:04.000
Noam Wolf: you know, just let it be. I don't want to touch the campaign. I would love to get to a place where every month I just put the same amount, my card is in there, I don't have to think about it, and I get leads, and I can focus on selling.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:25.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm. Yeah. No. Yeah, I definitely hear you, for sure. And, you know, when you put kind of the initial work into campaigns and into optimization, it can get to a spot where things are kind of, like, running a bit more on autopilot, right? There are still going to be different maintenance things, and it sounds like your bot may be able to help you with this, right, in terms of, like.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:43.000
Whitney Hodges: Uh, removing, uh, or adding negative keywords to, like, your Google campaign, so you're not showing up for, uh, you know, the wrong things. Um, you know, potentially on the meta ad side of things, just knowing when to turn an ad off if it's no longer performing, or launch a new creative if a refresh.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.000
Noam Wolf: Yeah.

00:18:43.000 --> 00:19:02.000
Whitney Hodges: is needed there. But, you know, a lot of times what we'll see on the meta ad side is when you can, like, come up with, like, a winning creative that's running, like, at different stages of your funnel of ads, because it's always reaching new people, right, in terms of the way that the targeting is set up.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:16.000
Whitney Hodges: um, it can run for months. Even, uh, you know, we've seen certain creatives run for, um, as long as, like, a year and a half, right, without changes needing to be made, um, and consistently, um, producing quality leads.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.000
Noam Wolf: Yeah.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.000
Noam Wolf: Wow.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:19.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm hmm. Yeah. Mm hmm.

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:24.000
